---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 22, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="AI Model Providers · Remy"
  description="The AI providers Remy relies on, the models each one runs, and what happens to your data at each."
>
  <header class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-8 sm:pt-12">
    <nav class="flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <img src="/remy-mark.png" alt="" class="h-7 w-7" />
        <span class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Remy</span>
      </a>
      <div class="hidden sm:flex items-center gap-5 text-sm text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
        <a href="/security" class="hover:text-[var(--ink)]">Security</a>
        <a href="/subprocessors" class="hover:text-[var(--ink)]">Subprocessors</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">AI model providers</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
      The providers Remy relies on, the models each one runs, and what happens to your data at
      each.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">
      <section class="space-y-3 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)]">
          The rule we hold providers to
        </h2>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-[var(--ink)]">No training on your data — at any provider, ever.</strong>
          Every provider that processes your conversations, mail, or calendar is contractually
          barred from training models on your data. Most of what Remy does runs under
          zero-data-retention terms: nothing is kept after your request completes. Where a lane
          runs on other terms — an enterprise arrangement, an exception request still pending —
          this page prints the exact state rather than rounding up. That includes the requests
          we have filed and not yet had granted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)]">Text and understanding</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--divider)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">Fireworks AI</span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--tint)] border border-[var(--tint-border)] px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--accent)]">Zero data retention</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
              Remy&rsquo;s primary inference provider. Runs the assistant you talk to
              (DeepSeek, with GLM as its sibling seat), the background readers that index and
              understand your mail and calendar (DeepSeek), image and document reading (Qwen),
              and search embeddings. No training on your data; nothing retained after the
              request. Read
              <a class="underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://docs.fireworks.ai/guides/security_compliance/data_handling">Fireworks&rsquo; data handling policy</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--divider)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">DeepInfra</span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--tint)] border border-[var(--tint-border)] px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--accent)]">Backup only</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
              Outage backup running the same models, so a provider outage degrades to the same
              brain on different servers — not a different assistant. No-training terms. Used
              only when Fireworks is unavailable. Read
              <a class="underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://docs.deepinfra.com/account/data-privacy">DeepInfra&rsquo;s data privacy policy</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--divider)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">Google (Gemini, enterprise API)</span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--surface-sunken)] border border-[var(--divider)] px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--ink-2)]">Rolling out &middot; exception pending</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
              The web-errand browser lane is moving to Gemini (decision August 22, 2026; it
              replaces the previous model on this lane). Terms: Google&rsquo;s paid enterprise
              API — no training on your data, your data not mixed with anyone else&rsquo;s.
              One item is not settled, so here it is plainly: Google&rsquo;s abuse monitoring
              can involve human review, and we have filed the exception request to remove it.
              Filed August 2026; not yet granted. This card updates when it is — or says so
              if it is refused. Read
              <a class="underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://cloud.google.com/gemini/docs/discover/data-governance">Google&rsquo;s enterprise data-governance terms</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)]">Voice</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--divider)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">Groq</span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--tint)] border border-[var(--tint-border)] px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--accent)]">Zero data retention</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
              Turns the mic button&rsquo;s dictation into text (Whisper). Zero-data-retention
              account. Read
              <a class="underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://console.groq.com/docs/your-data">Groq&rsquo;s data policy</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--divider)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">LiveKit &amp; Cartesia</span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--surface-sunken)] border border-[var(--divider)] px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--ink-2)]">Verification in progress</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
              Live voice conversations: LiveKit carries the session and transcribes your speech;
              Cartesia speaks Remy&rsquo;s replies. Both are configured not to train on your
              data; we are completing verification of their retention terms and will update this
              page with the result.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--divider)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">Retell AI (phone calls)</span>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--surface-sunken)] border border-[var(--divider)] px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--ink-2)]">Under review</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
              When Remy places a phone call for you, the in-call agent runs on Retell&rsquo;s
              stack, which uses an OpenAI model hosted by Retell and ElevenLabs voices. This
              lane predates our zero-retention standard and is under active review; calls are
              always placed with your explicit approval, and no mail or calendar content is
              shared with the call stack beyond what the call itself requires.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--ink)]">Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This page covers AI model providers. The full vendor list, including hosting and
          infrastructure, lives on the
          <a class="underline" href="/subprocessors">subprocessors</a> page. Questions:
          <a class="underline" href="mailto:privacy@hootventures.ai">privacy@hootventures.ai</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-[var(--line)] mt-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-8 flex items-center justify-between text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">
      <a class="hover:text-[var(--ink)]" href="/">&larr; Back to home</a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
        <a class="hover:text-[var(--ink)]" href="/why">Why Remy</a>
        <a class="hover:text-[var(--ink)]" href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
        <a class="hover:text-[var(--ink)]" href="/tos">Terms</a>
        <a class="hover:text-[var(--ink)]" href="mailto:support@hootventures.ai">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
